# BrightSmile Booking — Architecture (HLD)

Version: v1 (request 1 of requests.md) · Style: modular monolith (ADR-0001) · Status: proposed

## 1. Context and scope

BrightSmile Booking is a mobile-friendly website for BrightSmile Dental (2 clinics in Bengaluru, 6 dentists, about 450 appointments a week; a third clinic within 18 months). Patients sign in with a phone code and book, reschedule and cancel; reception runs each dentist's day, checks patients in and marks no-shows; patients get a confirmation and a reminder 24 hours before by SMS or WhatsApp; the practice manager sets hours and sees no-shows. Out of scope (non-goals, `scope.md`): insurance claims (REQ-020), a native app (REQ-021), online payment (REQ-022), clinical records (REQ-025), import of the paper diary (REQ-030), waiting lists, recalls, marketing messages, integration with the clinic's dental software, other languages, report export. Go-live is firm on 1 March 2027 (MVP); R2 follows about 2–3 weeks later.

| Actor | Kind (person / external system) | Interaction |
|---|---|---|
| act-patient | person | Signs in with a phone code, books for self and family, changes or cancels, receives messages |
| act-receptionist | person | Runs the day view of one clinic, books for callers and walk-ins, checks in, marks no-shows, lifts blocks |
| act-dentist | person | Views own day, read only |
| act-practice-manager | person | Sets hours, leave, treatments and staff accounts, reads the no-show report |
| act-sms-provider | external system | Sends SMS (sign-in code, confirmation, reminder) through DLT-registered templates, reports delivery and STOP replies |
| act-whatsapp-provider | external system | Sends WhatsApp template messages, reports delivery |

```mermaid
C4Context
title System context — BrightSmile Booking (v1)
Person(act_patient, "Patient", "Books from a phone")
Person(act_receptionist, "Receptionist", "Runs one clinic's day")
