## 3. Solution strategy

A **modular monolith** (ADR-0001): one API deployable with eight capability modules and one PostgreSQL database, plus a static single-page web app. It beats the next-simpler style (a layered monolith without module boundaries) because R2 modules (MOD-06, MOD-08) ship after the MVP and a third clinic must arrive as data (QA-011); it beats microservices because the two drivers need one transaction, not a saga (QA-003), and the team is small with a firm date (CON-001).

| Pattern | Driver that needs it | Where |
|---|---|---|
| Layers (entry, business, data) in the one deployable | Always | ctr-clinic-api |
| Database exclusion constraint on overlapping appointments (ADR-0003) | QA-003 | ent-appointment in ctr-db |
| Message rows with a precomputed send time, claimed by a dispatcher (ADR-0002, ADR-0009) | QA-004 | cmp-messaging, ent-message |
| Ports and adapters (ADR-0006), one adapter per external provider | QA-009, QA-004: two providers, one core | cmp-channel-adapters |
| Retry with backoff, timeout, circuit breaker on provider calls | QA-004, QA-005 | cmp-channel-adapters |
| Idempotent webhooks and idempotent sends | QA-004 | cmp-messaging, cmp-channel-adapters |
| Role-based access with clinic scoping in each module | QA-007 | cmp-identity and every module |
| Account and person split (ADR-0008) | FR-006, FR-025, PD-007 | ent-patient-account, ent-patient |
| Static CDN delivery, cookie session (ADR-0004) | QA-001, QA-010, QA-007 | ctr-web |

Not used, and why: no message broker (volume about 1,000 reminders a week, ADR-0002), no cache (live queries meet QA-001 at this size), no API gateway (one deployable), no CQRS or event sourcing (the history table in FR-024 is an audit log, not the source of state), no Kubernetes (ADR-0005).

## 4. Building blocks

Views: one container view (below) and one component view of ctr-clinic-api.

```mermaid
C4Container
title Containers — BrightSmile Booking (v1)
Person(act_patient, "Patient", "Books from a phone")
Person(act_receptionist, "Receptionist", "Runs one clinic's day")
Person(act_dentist, "Dentist", "Views own day")
Person(act_practice_manager, "Practice manager", "Sets hours, reads report")
System_Boundary(sys_booking, "BrightSmile Booking") {
Container(ctr_web, "Web app", "React SPA on CDN", "Screens for all four roles")
Container(ctr_clinic_api, "Clinic API", "Python FastAPI", "Booking, schedules, reminders")
ContainerDb(ctr_db, "Database", "PostgreSQL", "All appointment and patient data")
}
System_Ext(act_sms_provider, "SMS provider", "DLT-registered SMS")
System_Ext(act_whatsapp_provider, "WhatsApp provider", "Approved templates")
Rel(act_patient, ctr_web, "rel-001 Books, changes", "HTTPS")
Rel(act_receptionist, ctr_web, "rel-002 Runs the day", "HTTPS")
Rel(act_dentist, ctr_web, "rel-003 Views own day", "HTTPS")
Rel(act_practice_manager, ctr_web, "rel-004 Sets up, reports", "HTTPS")
Rel(ctr_web, ctr_clinic_api, "rel-005 Calls API", "HTTPS REST")
Rel(ctr_clinic_api, ctr_db, "rel-006 Reads, writes", "SQL over TLS")
Rel(ctr_clinic_api, act_sms_provider, "rel-007 Sends SMS", "HTTPS REST")
Rel(ctr_clinic_api, act_whatsapp_provider, "rel-008 Sends WhatsApp", "HTTPS REST")
Rel(act_sms_provider, ctr_clinic_api, "rel-009 Receipts, STOP", "Webhook")
Rel(act_whatsapp_provider, ctr_clinic_api, "rel-010 Receipts", "Webhook")
```

### Containers
| ID | Name | Kind | Technology | Responsibilities | Owns data | Buildable by backend agent |
|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|
| ctr-web | Web app | web front end (static) | React + TypeScript SPA, served from CDN | All screens for patient, receptionist, dentist and manager; mobile-first for patients; calls ctr-clinic-api only | none (holds no data; session is an `HttpOnly` cookie) | no |
| ctr-clinic-api | Clinic API | modular monolith API | Python 3.12, FastAPI, SQLAlchemy, Alembic | All business modules (section 4 components), the reminder dispatcher and the scheduled jobs, provider webhooks, `GET /health` | ent-clinic, ent-dentist, ent-treatment-type, ent-working-hours, ent-leave, ent-staff-account, ent-patient-account, ent-patient, ent-otp-challenge, ent-appointment, ent-appointment-event, ent-no-show-block, ent-message | yes |
| ctr-db | Database | relational data store | PostgreSQL 16 with `btree_gist`, managed, HA standby | Holds the tables of the entities above; enforces the no-overlap constraint (ADR-0003) | none (stores ctr-clinic-api's entities; only ctr-clinic-api connects) | no (managed infrastructure) |

### Components
ctr-clinic-api has 8 components (one component view).

| ID | Container | Name | Responsibility |
|---|---|---|---|
| cmp-identity | ctr-clinic-api | Identity and access | Patient phone-code sign-in and throttling, staff password sign-in, session tokens, RBAC and clinic scoping used by all modules, staff accounts, patient accounts, family members, channel choice and STOP flag, erasure on request. Serves FR-002, FR-003, FR-004, FR-005, FR-006, FR-013 (stores the choice), FR-031 (flag), NFR-006, NFR-007 |
| cmp-scheduling | ctr-clinic-api | Clinics, schedules and slots | Clinics, dentists, treatment types, weekly hours and breaks, leave and the "to move" list, free-slot calculation including "first available". Serves FR-001, FR-007, FR-008, FR-009, FR-010 |
| cmp-booking | ctr-clinic-api | Appointments | Owns appointments and their history; online book, reschedule, cancel with the 4-hour rule; reception-side book, move, cancel without it; status changes; patient's appointment list. Serves FR-011, FR-012, FR-015, FR-016, FR-017, FR-018, FR-020 (bookings), FR-024 |
| cmp-reception | ctr-clinic-api | Reception and dentist day | Day view per clinic, dentist's own day, patient search and create, arrived, no-show and undo, reminders-failed list. Serves FR-019, FR-020, FR-021, FR-022, FR-023, FR-033 |
| cmp-noshow-policy | ctr-clinic-api | Repeat no-show block | Counts a person's no-shows in 6 months, blocks and lifts online booking (R2). Serves FR-025, FR-026 |
| cmp-messaging | ctr-clinic-api | Messages and reminders | Builds confirmations, change notices, reminders and codes from templates; creates and cancels reminder rows with quiet-hours timing; dispatcher; fallback; STOP handling; reminder-failed state. Serves FR-013, FR-014, FR-018, FR-027, FR-028, FR-029, FR-030, FR-031, FR-033, NFR-005, NFR-011 |
| cmp-channel-adapters | ctr-clinic-api | Channel adapters | One adapter for the SMS provider and one for the WhatsApp provider: send, template mapping, error mapping, signature check and parsing of webhooks (anti-corruption layer). Serves FR-029, NFR-011 |
| cmp-reporting | ctr-clinic-api | No-show report | Monthly no-shows and rate per clinic for 12 months, read through cmp-booking (R2). Serves FR-032 |

```mermaid
