The diagram shows the calls that carry the design. Calls to `cmp-identity` for authorisation by every module, the webhook path into `cmp-channel-adapters` and `cmp-messaging` (rel-009, rel-010), and the SQL of `cmp-noshow-policy` are described in the tables, to stay within the diagram limit.

## 5. Data

Conceptual only; tables, columns and indexes are in `data-model.md`. Every entity has one owner; other components use its interface.

| ID | Entity | Owner (container or component) | Key attributes (mark PII / sensitive) | Store | Retention |
|---|---|---|---|---|---|
| ent-clinic | Clinic | cmp-scheduling | name, address, phone, active | ctr-db | Kept |
| ent-dentist | Dentist | cmp-scheduling | name (PII), active | ctr-db | Kept; anonymised 24 months after deactivation |
| ent-treatment-type | Treatment type | cmp-scheduling | name, duration minutes, online flag, active | ctr-db | Kept |
| ent-working-hours | Weekly working hours and breaks | cmp-scheduling | dentist, clinic, weekday, start, end, breaks | ctr-db | Kept |
| ent-leave | Dentist leave | cmp-scheduling | dentist, start, end (whole or part day) | ctr-db | 24 months |
| ent-staff-account | Staff account | cmp-identity | username, role, clinic (receptionist), dentist link, name (PII), password hash (sensitive), active | ctr-db | Kept while active; anonymised 24 months after deactivation |
| ent-patient-account | Patient account (a phone number) | cmp-identity | phone number (PII), name (PII), preferred channel, reminders opt-out | ctr-db | Until deletion on request (30 days) |
| ent-patient | Patient (a person, the account holder or a family member) | cmp-identity | name (PII), birth year (PII), account, active | ctr-db | Until deletion on request; anonymised at 24 months idle |
| ent-otp-challenge | Sign-in code | cmp-identity | phone (PII), code hash (sensitive), expiry, attempts, locked until | ctr-db | 24 hours |
| ent-appointment | Appointment | cmp-booking | clinic, dentist, patient, treatment, start, end, status, channel, booked by | ctr-db | 24 months, then personal link removed |
| ent-appointment-event | Appointment history | cmp-booking | appointment, from and to status, actor, time, reason | ctr-db | Same as its appointment |
| ent-no-show-block | Repeat no-show block | cmp-noshow-policy | patient, blocked at, lifted by, lifted at | ctr-db | 24 months |
| ent-message | Message and reminder | cmp-messaging | kind, channel, patient account, appointment, due and scheduled times, status, provider message id, attempts; rendered text holds name and phone (PII) | ctr-db | 90 days, then deleted |

Consistency: all components share one database and one transaction, so every cross-component write is **strong** (a booking, its history row, the reminder row and a block check commit together). The only eventual consistency is toward providers: a message row is committed first and delivered by the dispatcher, with a staleness bound of 15 minutes for reminders (QA-004) and about 30 seconds for confirmations and codes. Delivery status arrives later by webhook (eventual, minutes).

Backup / RPO / RTO: ctr-db, continuous log archiving with point-in-time restore and a daily snapshot kept 14 days, encrypted; RPO 15 minutes, RTO 1 hour (ASM-007), tested by a restore before go-live. HA standby in a second zone. ctr-web is rebuilt from source; it has no data.

## 6. Integration and APIs

| ID | From | To | Purpose | Protocol | Sync/async | Contract | Auth | Resilience (timeout, retry, breaker, fallback) |
|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|
| rel-001 | act-patient | ctr-web | Patient screens | HTTPS | sync | none (browser) | none until sign-in | CDN; no dynamic dependency |
| rel-002 | act-receptionist | ctr-web | Reception screens | HTTPS | sync | none (browser) | none until sign-in | as rel-001 |
| rel-003 | act-dentist | ctr-web | Dentist day screen | HTTPS | sync | none (browser) | none until sign-in | as rel-001 |
| rel-004 | act-practice-manager | ctr-web | Manager screens | HTTPS | sync | none (browser) | none until sign-in | as rel-001 |
| rel-005 | ctr-web | ctr-clinic-api | All application operations | HTTPS REST/JSON under `/api` | sync | api-clinic-api-v1 | JWT in `HttpOnly` cookie, CSRF header on writes | Client timeout 10 s, read retried once, writes never retried automatically (booking conflict is a normal answer) |
| rel-006 | ctr-clinic-api | ctr-db | Reads and writes | SQL over TLS | sync | none (database) | DB credentials from secret store | Pool, statement timeout 5 s, retry of read-only statements once, HA failover |
| rel-007 | ctr-clinic-api | act-sms-provider | Sends codes, confirmations, reminders | HTTPS REST | async (dispatcher) except sign-in code, sent in request | provider API (see `integration-specs.md`) | Provider API key | Timeout 5 s, 3 attempts with backoff (5 s, 30 s) inside the 15-minute window, circuit breaker after 5 failures in 1 minute, message stays queued |
| rel-008 | ctr-clinic-api | act-whatsapp-provider | Sends template messages | HTTPS REST | async (dispatcher) | provider API (see `integration-specs.md`) | Provider API key | As rel-007; on final failure falls back once to SMS (FR-029) when the switch is on |
| rel-009 | act-sms-provider | ctr-clinic-api | Delivery receipts, STOP replies | HTTPS webhook | async | api-clinic-api-v1 (webhook operations) | HMAC signature with shared secret | Provider retries; handler idempotent on provider message id; always answers quickly |
| rel-010 | act-whatsapp-provider | ctr-clinic-api | Delivery receipts | HTTPS webhook | async | api-clinic-api-v1 (webhook operations) | HMAC signature with shared secret | As rel-009 |

### Contracts
| ID | Owner | File | Version |
|---|---|---|---|
| api-clinic-api-v1 | ctr-clinic-api | contracts/clinic-api-v1.openapi.yaml | 1.0.0 |

### Events
No asynchronous messaging. The `ent-message` table is a work list inside the one database (ADR-0002), not an event stream.

