## 8. Deployment

Every environment hosts every container; staging and dev use the smallest tiers.

| Environment | Node | Kind | Hosts (container ids) | Replicas / scaling |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| dev | Static site bucket and CDN | managed static hosting | ctr-web | 1 |
| dev | Container service | managed container platform | ctr-clinic-api | 1 replica |
| dev | Database | managed PostgreSQL, single node | ctr-db | 1, no standby |
| staging | Static site bucket and CDN | managed static hosting | ctr-web | 1 |
| staging | Container service | managed container platform | ctr-clinic-api | 1 replica, provider sandbox accounts |
| staging | Database | managed PostgreSQL, single node | ctr-db | 1, no standby |
| prod | CDN and load balancer with WAF | managed edge | ctr-web (static), routes `/api` to ctr-clinic-api | managed |
| prod | Container service, zones A and B | managed container platform | ctr-clinic-api | 2 replicas, one per zone, scale 2–4 on CPU above 60% |
| prod | Database, zones A and B | managed PostgreSQL with HA standby | ctr-db | 1 primary, 1 synchronous standby |

```mermaid
flowchart TB
%% Production deployment — BrightSmile Booking (v1)
internet["Browsers and providers"]
subgraph region["Cloud region in India"]
  subgraph edge["Edge"]
    node_cdn["CDN, load balancer, WAF: ctr-web static files"]
  end
  subgraph zone_a["Zone A"]
    node_api_a["ctr-clinic-api replica 1"]
    node_db_primary["ctr-db primary"]
  end
  subgraph zone_b["Zone B"]
    node_api_b["ctr-clinic-api replica 2"]
