## 12. Risks and technical debt

The Risk & Dependency agent expands these into `risk-register.md`, with the same ids.

| ID | Risk | Likelihood | Impact | Mitigation |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| RSK-001 | SMS DLT registration or WhatsApp template approval is late (DEP-001, DEP-002), so confirmations, reminders and sign-in codes cannot go live on 1 March 2027 (CON-001) | Medium | High | Provider test accounts in weeks 1–2; templates written and submitted early; staging uses sandbox providers; the clinic owns registration with our help (A-005) |
| RSK-002 | Sign-in codes and reminders depend on one SMS provider (outage blocks sign-in), and code floods cost money (thr-008, thr-014) | Medium | Medium | 7-day session, per-phone and per-IP limits, daily cap, circuit breaker, alert, reception takes bookings by phone as before |
| RSK-003 | Q-007 answered differently: families need separate sign-ins on one phone, which phone-code sign-in cannot do; MOD-01 grows 2–4 person-days | Medium | Medium | Account and person already split (ADR-0008); FR-006 is R2 |
| RSK-004 | Reminder dispatcher shares the API process (ADR-0002); a slow provider, deploy or crash delays reminders beyond 15 minutes | Medium | High | Async sends with 5 s timeout, 2 replicas, claim with skip locked, lag alert at 10 minutes, nightly reconciliation (JOB-005), option to move the same code into a worker |
| RSK-005 | WhatsApp-to-SMS fallback is not agreed by the client (ISS-001, ASM-005) and adds message charges | Medium | Low | Built behind a switch, delivered in R2, default on per SA-008; client confirms |
| RSK-006 | Performance and availability targets are our proposals (ISS-004, ASM-006) and the no-show baseline is unknown (ISS-003) | Medium | Low | Confirm at Gate 2; measure from go-live; first 2 months of data as baseline |
| RSK-007 | Deleting a patient on request (NFR-007) conflicts with keeping appointment counts for the no-show report and block | Low | Medium | Anonymise rather than delete the appointment row; deletion removes name, phone, birth year and messages; report counts stay |
| RSK-008 | Hosting and domain not fixed (Q-008); a client-mandated host changes service names and cost | Medium | Low | Cloud-agnostic shape of three managed service kinds (ADR-0005); confirm before staging set-up |
| RSK-009 | A person who takes over or SIM-swaps a phone number can sign in as that patient (thr-003, ADR-0007) | Low | Medium | Accepted; minimal data shown, no clinical data, lockouts; reception can deactivate an account |
| RSK-010 | Reception types the paper diary into the system before go-live (DEP-006, SA-005); errors or delay mean double-booked or missing visits on day one | Medium | Medium | Same booking screens with the no-overlap constraint; a dry run in the week before; reception checks each day's list against the paper diary for a week |

